<onlyinclude>The '''semiosphere''' is Yuri Lotman's concept of the cultural environment in which sign processes occur. It emphasizes that communication and meaning depend on relations among languages, texts and cultural practices rather than isolated signs alone.

== Explanation ==
A translation between two languages illustrates a boundary in such an environment. Translation can change which distinctions are available, while familiar signs can be interpreted differently outside their original setting. Lotman's metaphor describes cultural organization, not a measurable shell surrounding Earth.

